{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.KashaevCSigma","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.KashaevCSigma","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.KashaevAsymptoticBounds","lean:module:QOU.OneLoopPrefactorInvariance"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_cot_saddle_div_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_cot_saddle_div_two","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevCSigma.lean#L130-L137","doc":"**The number `hτ` has to produce.**  `|cot θ*|/2 = √3/2`.\n\nStated so the remaining gap is a definite claim in Lean rather than prose:\n`hτ` asserts `|τ_DG(4₁)| = √3/2`, which is Dimofte–Garoufalidis' own worked\nfigure-eight example and is, in this corpus, a numerical result only. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.k_sq_eq_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.k_sq_eq_half","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevCSigma.lean#L99-L109","doc":"**`k = 2^{−1/2}` too**, with `hc` supplied.  The Hessian cancels between\n`c_σ` and `|τ|` before it is ever evaluated — so this never depended on\n`cot θ* = −√3`, on the trace field, or on which manifold this is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.cSigma_saddle_pow_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.cSigma_saddle_pow_four","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevCSigma.lean#L87-L97","doc":"**`c_σ⁴ = 1/3`, with `hc` supplied rather than assumed.**\n\n`OneLoopPrefactorInvariance.c_pow_four_eq_third` is applied here with its `hc`\ndischarged by `cSigma_sq_mul_abs_cot` — so the chain from the Kashaev sum to\n`c_σ = 3^{−1/4}` no longer passes through an assumption. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.cot_saddle_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.cot_saddle_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevCSigma.lean#L80-L85","doc":"The saddle's cotangent is nonzero — what `cSigma_sq_mul_abs_cot` needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.cSigma_saddle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.cSigma_saddle","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevCSigma.lean#L73-L78","doc":"`c_σ(5π/6) = 1/√√3 = 3^{−1/4}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.stirling_mul_gaussWidth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.stirling_mul_gaussWidth","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevCSigma.lean#L55-L71","doc":"**The link back to the analysis.**  Step 7's Stirling factor `2N sin θ`\ntimes steps 12–19's Gaussian width `√(π/a)` at `a = π|cot θ|/N` is exactly\n`c_σ(θ)·N^{3/2}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.cSigma_sq_mul_abs_cot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.cSigma_sq_mul_abs_cot","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevCSigma.lean#L43-L53","doc":"**`hc`, derived.**  The Hessian cancels between the two ingredients.\n\nThis is the hypothesis `OneLoopPrefactorInvariance` assumed; it is an identity\nfor the `c_σ` the analysis actually produces, at any angle where `cot θ ≠ 0`.\nNothing about `4₁` enters. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.cSigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.cSigma","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevCSigma.lean#L38-L41","doc":"**The one-loop constant, in the shape the asymptotics produce it.**\nStirling factor over the square root of the Hessian. ","signatureChunk":0}]}